WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.480
Pick leaves from plants
growing in the shade,

2
00:00:02.530 --> 00:00:04.820
and from plants growing in the sun.

3
00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:06.620
Measure every one.

4
00:00:06.670 --> 00:00:09.640
On average, the shade
leaves come out bigger.

5
00:00:09.690 --> 00:00:11.450
But is that gap real?

6
00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:14.330
Or could the difference
be due to chance alone?

7
00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:18.100
So how big must the gap
be before you believe it?

8
00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:23.460
In this mission, you'll meet the t-test,
a test built to compare two means.

9
00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:27.830
Then you'll run it on limpet shells from
an exposed shore and a sheltered one,

10
00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:29.440
and reach a verdict.

11
00:00:29.490 --> 00:00:34.930
Your mission: decide how big a gap
must be before you believe it, and why.
